<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95260" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκυθ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>behave like a Scythian</i>, i.e., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>drink immoderately</i>, Hieronym.Rhod. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.499f
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπισκυθίζω</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> from the Scythian
			practice of scalping slain enemies, <i>shave the head</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσκυθισμένος ξυρῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					241
				</span></i>
			; so [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαίτην] ἐσκύθιξε φασγάνῳ</span>
			<i>cut</i> it <i>off</i> in mourning, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				790.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Achaea</span>): cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποσκυθίζω</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>talk Scythian</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Him.
				<u>Or.</u>
				30.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>